    dcterms:description "Monitors delivery timeliness, service quality metrics, regulatory adherence, and documentation completeness for community service programs subject to federal, state, or contract compliance requirements. Community services organizations that receive public funding operate under strict delivery timelines — SNAP must be issued within 30 days of application, housing assistance waitlist notifications have required timeframes, and case documentation must be current for billing and audit purposes. Output at [972:976] feeds the Service Delivery Integrity Monitor." ;
